.TH CWE-456 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-456 \- Missing Initialization of a Variable
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not initialize critical variables, which causes the execution environment to use unexpected values.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2026\-46300
Linux Kernel, added 2026\-10\-28.
.PP
Linux Kernel Missing Initialization of a Variable Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Linux Kernel contains a missing initialization of a variable vulnerability that could allow for unintended modification of page\-cache\-backed data via failure to preserve the shared\-fragment marker during socket buffer coalescing, causing ESP input processing to decrypt shared fragments in place. This vulnerability can be chained with CVE\-2026\-109618 and CVE\-2026\-109619 to implant PHP webshells and run commands as root.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply vendor mitigations; follow CISA BOD 26\-04 (risk\-based patching) and forensics triage. Discontinue use if no mitigation exists.
 Due 2026\-10\-31.
.PP
